        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fanny Talbot, John Ruskin\n- Roles: landowner, philanthropist, art critic, art patron, draughtsman, watercolourist, social thinker\n\nFacts:\n- John Ruskin was born on 8 February 1819 and died on 20 January 1900.\n- Fanny Talbot, née Browne, was born in 1824 and died in 1917.\n- John Ruskin was the leading English art critic of the Victorian era.\n- John Ruskin was also an art patron, draughtsman, watercolourist, prominent social thinker, and philanthropist.\n- Fanny Talbot was a landowner and philanthropist.\n- Fanny Talbot was a friend and correspondent of John Ruskin.",
